msgid "False. Most machine learning problems are solved very efficiently by classical algorithms and quantum algorithms are not likely to offer any substantial speed-up. The goal in QML is to finding datasets with features that are well-described by quantum states and/or to find mappings of data features that optimize the accuracy of models.\n"
